    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our clear priority. He faces Arrighetti in a prime matchup where his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the opposing pitcher's slow delivery\u2014which significantly boosts his stolen base expectancy\u2014create an elite offensive ceiling. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) follow closely behind; both benefit from a generous park factor and a favorable SP xERA of 4.46 against Ginn, allowing them to capitalize on high-leverage spots in the batting order. **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also presents a strong play, as the 4.93 xERA of Littell provides the perfect runway for him to maximize his base-running speed and contact profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung** (41.87) and **Brayan Rocchio** (41.06). While both hovered near the marginal start threshold, their scores were suppressed by encounters with elite-tier arms (Murphy and Montgomery, both < 3.00 xERA). Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor of **Heliot Ramos** (44.20) and the positional stacking benefits of our primary starters. We remain cautious with **Heliot Ramos**, whose score remains the lowest in the starting lineup due to a stiff matchup against Woo and a negative park factor; he is on a short leash to ensure we preserve our daily game caps if he fails to produce early. While we are running with a high-ceiling core, **Drake Baldwin** (58.04) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.98) face slightly more resilient arms in Gore and Martin, making them pivot points for our overall performance today.",
